:"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:24815","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":24145,"name":"Babel"},{"id":28692,"name":"Aez"},{"id":662610,"name":"Sigurbjörn Thorgrimsson"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/24815-Biogen","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.myspace.com/biogenmusic","https://weirdcore.bandcamp.com/","https://soundcloud.com/biogen","https://www.facebook.com/icelandbiogen"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2638508/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2638508","image":"https://i.discogs.com/PJ7eGl0DdiaMFwQzTQOhGyM3t07mUjKBK40szFZa58k/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:450/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI2Mzg1/MDgtMTU5MzAzMzgy/Ny0yOTYzLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/DwMCRFPm72ur0KDsven8fBFIG-pI2RbSmj8_SUjBFUU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI2Mzg1/MDgtMTU5MzAzMzgy/Ny0yOTYzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2638508","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":10509781,"name":"Tobias Hinz"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2638508-Phazer-6","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.instagram.com/herrmanhinz","https://soundcloud.com/phazer"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/30017/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"30017","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Xea6aVO0xR39XFNLXL3OZShHQoWHI8wvA1khELaHGWo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:402/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMwMDE3/LTE3NjA4ODI2Mjct/MjEzOS5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/_1HsEN8YltJ-P-qXCzUhsRWv8R_EFDi9we3MkpLEcOE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTMwMDE3/LTE3NjA4ODI2Mjct/MjEzOS5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Pete Rock & C.L. Smooth were a hip-hop duo from Mount Vernon, New York. They made their debut with their 1991 EP, All Souled Out and followed with 1992's Mecca and the Soul Brother LP.\r\nAs a producer, DJ Pete Rock (Peter Phillips) tended to prefer obscure soul and jazz sides for sample sources, frequently making use of horn-driven hooks. Lead vocalist CL Smooth (Corey Penn) tended to be philosophical in his raps, and he mostly avoided profanity. Their signature hit was “They Reminisce Over You (T.R.O.Y.)”, a dirge for fallen friends--namely Troy \"Trouble T-Roy\" Dixon, a member of Heavy D & The Boyz, who died in 1990.\r\n1994's The Main Ingredient was the follow up, and they appeared on a string of guest appearances for remixes, soundtracks, and other works. Public Enemy, EPMD, Heavy D and Johnny Gill were among the artists they collaborated with, and they can also claim credit for producing (and performing on) Run-DMC’s 1993 comeback single 'Down with the King'. Despite all this, the duo failed to go gold on any of their own releases.\r\nSeparating in 1995 (shortly after a Sprite TV commercial), they eventually reunited on a handful of cuts from Pete Rock’s solo recordings: Soul Survivor (1998), PeteStrumentals (2001) and Soul Survivor II (2004). They also went on a brief reunion tour as a warm up for their then-anticipated new album, which ended with a show at London's famous Jazz Cafe. Despite these intermittent collaborations, the pair has exchanged dismissive comments toward each other in separate interviews, disavowing plans for a full-fledged reunion.\r\nTheir best-of compilation, Good Life, was released on Elektra in 2003.\r\nA deluxe CD box-set of Mecca and the Soul Brother was released in October 2010 by Traffic, a division of Elektra. The package includes a remastered CD of the original album, a second disc of remixes, instrumentals and acapellas, a fold-out poster and a detailed booklet with interviews and insights from Rock and Smooth. (courtesy wikipedia)\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:30017","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":246265,"name":"Pete Phillips"},{"active":true,"id":691383,"name":"Corey Penn"}],"namevariations":